`--stub-macro` pins a config-declared macro to a literal for the whole render — preamble and step
body alike — and short-circuits it before any subprocess starts. The declared argv is `false`, which
exits 1: had the command run, the render would carry the macro's failure instead of the stamp.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  macros:
    build: ["false"]
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-macro-stub/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-macro-stub
title: Macro Stub
summary: Macro pinned by --stub-macro.
jinja: true
inline_steps: true
---

Preamble stamp {{ macro('core.macros.build') }}.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-macro-stub/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  one: []
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-macro-stub/one/prompt.md --
---
name: one
summary: Only step.
---

Body stamp {{ macro('core.macros.build') }}.
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-macro-stub --stub-macro core.macros.build=19700101
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
Preamble stamp 19700101.

